The second factor kept when other preferences are saved (phpMyAdmin issue 19900, "two
factor auth disappears"). UserPreferences::save() writes the whole set of preferences
of the user, and the settings of a page (PageSettings) and the reset of
/preferences/manage gave it one with no 2fa: the two-factor authentication went away
with them, with no new authentication, as through /config/set (CVE-2026-119429, vuxml
e6b90d23-d49d-11f1-bae2-3497f65b111b). Now save() keeps the stored 2fa when the set it
is given has none; the page of two-factor authentication still takes it away (it saves
a 2fa with no backend), after the second factor.

Upstream, in QA_5_2 (5.2.4, not released) and master; this is UserPreferences.php of
QA_5_2 against 5.2.3 (git diff RELEASE_5_2_3 QA_5_2):
- 889af69af89f78c02d4d9558524b62c0fd2191be, efturtle, 07.11.2025: "Preserve 2FA settings
  when saving partial user preferences"
- 88608105b96dfd715a6470e3a4c782e02ac3d95a, efturtle, 07.11.2025: "Fix 2FA preservation
  for both session and database storage"
  (both pull request 19925, merged in 4de9f0f0b1bd on 17.12.2025)
- daa9d1e252f9e4f49b8047453c6fd7bf1abfa94c, Maurício Meneghini Fauth, 24.01.2026: "Fix
  case where user preferences are not removed", pull request 20047 (merged in
  b1cec4e48f09): only the 2fa is kept, not the rest of what was stored
